conditions:
In most cases, our legal basis will be one of the following:
Contractual necessity: where it is necessary to process personal data in order to perform an agreement with you or to enter into such an agreement (for example, processing data in order to provide the scanning service);
Legal obligation: where we are under a legal obligation to process your personal data in order to comply with laws and regulations;
Legitimate interests: where we have a reasonable basis to process your personal data and that basis is reasonable when weighed against your rights and interests;
Consent: where you have consented to our processing of your data;
Substantial public interest: where we process sensitive or special categories of data (i.e., data revealing or relating to a person’s health, ethnicity, political opinions, religious beliefs, sexual orientation or other protected characteristics) and the processing is in the substantial public interest (for example, to provide support to vulnerable customers).
